   "he": "״שְׁבוּעָה שֶׁלֹּא אוֹכְלֶנָּה״, וַאֲכָלָהּ – אֵינוֹ חַיָּיב אֶלָּא אַחַת כּוּ׳. הָא תּוּ לְמָה לִי?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If one says: On my oath I will not eat this loaf, and he then says again: On my oath I will not eat it, and again: On my «oath I will not eat it, and he» then «ate it, he is liable only once.» The Gemara asks: «Why do I» need the mishna to mention «this additional,» third, oath: I will not eat it?"
